{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"mesodermic-vaporish-seaslug","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe store-wide compaction sweep stalls every writer in the fleet for minutes at a time. Live\noperator profiling: \"the compaction spawns a fresh git log --full-history child every few\nseconds (7268 → 7496 …), each at ~100% CPU, holding the global write lock throughout.\"\n\nCause, confirmed in code. `_compact_locked` builds the SNAPSHOT authorship ledger via\n`_build_authorship_ledger` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py:72`), which calls\n`authorship.build_ticket_position_commit_map` (`src/rebar/attest/authorship.py:294`) — one\n`git log --full-history` walk PER TICKET, executed INSIDE the store write lock.\n\nThis is bug 7084 recurring one scale up. 7084 found the same walk running per SIGNED EVENT\n(6.78s/event on a 71,041-commit branch; 47.5s of a 48.1s compact-on-close whose real mutation\nis ~0.4s) and batched it to per-TICKET (0.53s for an 18-file ticket, 3.83s for a 159-file one).\nThat was right for compact-on-close, which folds one ticket. Story\n`gaudy-gangrenous-basilisk` made `compact-all` the store's standing sweep, so the same call now\nruns once per ticket across thousands of tickets — per-ticket became the new per-event.\n\nTwo secondary defects in the same path:\n- `_commit_backfill` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact.py:275`) stages with an unscoped\n  `git add -A`, so a concurrent writer's in-flight event files can be committed under the\n  compactor's \"chore: backfill SNAPSHOT files\" message.\n- `compact_trigger.run_sweep` probes `write_lock_is_busy` once before the loop, so a long sweep\n  never re-yields to writers that arrive mid-run.\n\n## Approach\nBatch the read-only prep with no lock held, then take short lock windows for mutations only.\n\n**1. Hoist the history walk out of the lock.** `git log` is read-only and never needed the\nwrite lock. Resolve the ledger's introducing-commit data before acquiring; then lock, re-check\nthe ticket's event set is unchanged, write the SNAPSHOT, retire sources, commit, release. Same\nverify-outside-lock discipline as the original P0 fix, one layer down. A changed event set means\nthe prepared fold is stale — abort that ticket cleanly and let the next pass take it.\n\n**2. Amortize the walk with the primitive that already exists.** Do not write a new batcher:\n`authorship.build_introducing_commit_map` (`src/rebar/attest/authorship.py:388`) already maps\nEVERY tracker event path to its introducing commit in a SINGLE pass — O(events + history),\nmeasured ~2s at real store scale, validated against the per-event resolver with 0 mismatches\nover 700 sampled events, and it keeps `resolve_event_commit` as a fail-closed fallback for\npaths it misses. Build it ONCE per sweep and query it per ticket, replacing N directory-scoped\nwalks with one. Hours become seconds.\n\nWith the walk gone from the critical section, the per-ticket lock window is the SNAPSHOT write,\nthe renames and the commit — the ~0.4s that 7084's own measurement attributed to real mutation.\nThat subsumes chunking: the hold is already bounded by one ticket's mutation.\n\n**3. Scope the staging and re-yield.** Commit only the paths the sweep folded rather than\n`git add -A`, and re-probe `write_lock_is_busy` between tickets so a sweep that began on a quiet\nstore stands aside when writers arrive.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py` — accept a prebuilt commit map; hoist ledger prep out of\n  the locked section; re-check the event set under the lock.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact.py` — build the map once per sweep and thread it through; scope\n  `_commit_backfill`'s staging to the folded paths.\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py` — re-probe the store lock between tickets.\n- `tests/unit/test_compact_sweep_perf.py` — new tests.\n\n## Testing\n- A sweep over N tickets performs ONE history walk, not N — asserted by counting calls to the\n  map builder, not by timing.\n- No `git log` child is spawned while the store write lock is held — asserted structurally, by\n  instrumenting the lock and the walk, never by a duration.\n- An event appended to a ticket between prep and the locked re-check aborts that ticket's fold\n  cleanly, writes no SNAPSHOT, and leaves its events live for the next pass.\n- The ledger produced with a prebuilt map is byte-identical to the one produced by the\n  per-ticket walk, over a store containing signed, unsigned and forged-signature events.\n- `_commit_backfill` commits only the folded paths: a concurrent writer's uncommitted event file\n  present during the sweep is NOT included in the compaction commit.\n- A sweep re-yields: with the store lock taken after the sweep starts, it stops folding further\n  tickets and leaves the rest live.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A store-wide sweep performs exactly one introducing-commit history walk regardless of\n      ticket count — a test counts builder invocations across a multi-ticket sweep.\n- [ ] No history walk runs inside the store write lock — a test instruments both and asserts\n      no walk observes the lock held.\n- [ ] A ticket whose events change between prep and the locked re-check is skipped cleanly:\n      no SNAPSHOT, no retired sources, events still live, exit 0.\n- [ ] The authorship ledger is unchanged by the optimisation — a test compares ledgers built\n      with and without the prebuilt map on signed, unsigned and forged-signature events.\n- [ ] The compaction commit contains only folded paths — a test asserts a concurrent writer's\n      uncommitted event file is not swept into it.\n- [ ] A sweep stands aside mid-run when a writer takes the lock, leaving remaining tickets\n      unfolded — and the full local gate set plus CI's pytest tiers pass.","id":"0d15-59a4-e140-444b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Sweep walks full git history per ticket under the store lock"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786647486795174001,"uuid":"2eaa40e2-1243-4e17-a8be-950f9df21c75"}